```javascript
const parser = new DOMParser();
const fragmentContainingDsd = parser.parseFromString(htmlWithDSD,
    'text/html', {declarativeShadowRoots: true});
```

In other words, to parse HTML that contains declarative shadow DOM. It's super-unfortunate that my example above wasn't just `el.innerHTML = htmlWithDSD` but we have https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/912 to deal with. [This section](https://github.com/mfreed7/declarative-shadow-dom/blob/master/README.md#potential-html-sanitizer-bypass) of the explainer summarizes the details.

